    "body": "@davidkna You may find this discussion interesting https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/1314/files#r438516719\r\n\r\nIt looked like this in its original form:\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/3ebd2c0ad508bd597e1821a580b1a78c18a3a4f1/install/install.sh#L117\r\n\r\nThen I came and broke it:\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/30ff5913bea6cb209ba55f3064c109853d45d521/install/install.sh#L117\r\n\r\nThen @chipbuster came and fix it:\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/6ecabdfee4a059c473a8a92073b0db58f8efaa02/install/install.sh#L117\r\n(This is the origin of the discussion linked earlier.)\r\n\r\nThen @dmccaffery changed it to its current form:\r\nhttps://github.com/starship/starship/blob/d1b2723033b247854166a0506a160e9ff62ec822/install/install.sh#L123-L124\r\n(This in fact originates from old PR of mine https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/1315/files#diff-65845b92f5ee07169285791a57b33dd35b5792a60a4d436d2c761324a492a2c1R98-R99)\r\n\r\nSo I'm pretty much responsible for this mess :upside_down_face: \r\n\r\nWith that being said I believe I had the right idea back then https://github.com/starship/starship/pull/1314/files#r438516719\r\nIf I try to update that to match the current state of code I get something along these lines:\r\n```suggestion\r\n      flags=$(test -n \"${VERBOSE-}\" && echo \"xzv\" || echo \"xz\")\r\n      ${sudo} tar -\"${flags}\"f \"${archive}\" -C \"${bin_dir}\"\r\n```\r\nWhat do you think about that?",
